        "thought_text": "Analyze the board's shape and connectivity. Instead of focusing solely on the number of free cells, consider the overall structure of the board, including any isolated regions or patterns that might prevent tiling. This approach can help identify cases where the board configuration is inherently unsolvable, even if the total number of free cells is correct.",
